<!--
  Launcher icon, foreground layer. Original work, Copyright (C) 2026 Eyed.

  The mark: a slab-serif "T" whose crossbar is a horseshoe moustache. Thragg
  is the app's namesake, the moustache is the one thing everybody remembers
  about him, and a "T" with a moustache for a crossbar is the whole name in
  one glyph. It is drawn from geometry — a bar, two hooked ends, a stem, a
  notch — not from any panel of the comic, so it depicts nobody and carries
  nobody's trademark. It replaced the prompt-chevron-and-cursor mark, which
  said "an editor" but said nothing about *this* one.

  Rejected in front of a renderer, at 48dp, on light and dark backdrops,
  squircle-masked:

  * An arched moustache with a stem read as a bridge or a mushroom.
  * The moustache alone read as any moustache, or as a magnet at 48dp.
  * A red stem under the bone moustache read as a tongue.

  So it is one tone, bone, and the crossbar is heavier than the stem so the
  moustache leads and the "T" follows. The notch at the top centre is what
  makes a bar a moustache: without it the same shape is a hanger.

  Geometry, since it is load-bearing and someone will want to re-cut it. The
  adaptive canvas is 108x108, the launcher shows the middle 72x72, and every
  mask shape fits inside the middle 66x66 circle. Ink spans x 30..78 and
  y 33..75 — 48 x 42, dead centred on (54,54) — and its furthest on-path point
  from the centre is 28.3, clearing the 33-unit safe radius on every mask. The
  bar is 10 units thick, the hooks 8 wide and 21 deep to their round ends, the
  stem 8.6 wide with a 4.3 radius foot, the notch 9.6 wide and 3.6 deep. Every
  curve is an axis-aligned quarter turn (the round ends are two of them), so
  the shape is bounded exactly by its own points, which LauncherIconTest
  relies on.
-->
